Chapter: LensQueryTest
  cites Data chapter Catalog
  cites Data chapter Schema
  cites Data chapter Row
  cites Data chapter RelAlgebra
  cites Data chapter Executor
  cites Data chapter Optimizer
  cites Lens chapter LensModel
  cites Lens chapter LensPlan

 The star: four users, twelve orders, amounts in cents. Per-user
 revenue: Alice 1500 + 5000 + 800 + 1500 = 8800, Bob 800 + 1500 +
 5000 = 7300, Carol 1500 + 800 + 5000 = 7300, Dave 5000 + 1500 =
 6500. Revenue by city: Springfield is Alice plus Carol = 16100,
 Shelbyville is Bob = 7300, Capital City is Dave = 6500. Credit
 limits live one per user: Alice 10000, Bob 20000, Carol 30000, Dave
 40000, so total credit by city is Springfield 40000, Shelbyville
 20000, Capital City 40000.

 The second query is the fan-out case this planner exists to kill: a
 user-grain measure (sum of users.credit-limit) asked alongside a
 fact-grain measure (sum of orders.amount), both by city. A naive
 engine joins users to orders first and sums the joined rows, which
 duplicates each user's credit limit once per order: Alice 4 orders x
 10000 + Carol 3 x 30000 = 130000 for Springfield, Bob 3 x 20000 =
 60000 for Shelbyville, Dave 2 x 40000 = 80000 for Capital City,
 all wrong. The grain-correct answers are 40000, 20000, and 40000,
 and this test asserts them. The planner gets them by aggregating
 credit at the users grain (no join at all) and revenue at the orders
 grain before any join, then equi-joining the two aggregated results
 on city.

 Sorting is ascending in CCE code order, and CCE assigns letters by
 frequency (etaoinshrdlcumwfgypbvkjxqz), therefore Shelbyville sorts
 before Springfield and Capital City sorts last. The spike pinned the
 same collation.

 The fourth query asks for several measures across several dimensions
 at once: total credit and revenue by city and user name. The old
 planner refused the shape with diagnostic 26 because measure results
 combined through a single-column equi-join; the combine step now
 joins on the full dimension column set, so the shape plans. Each
 city-and-name pair names exactly one user here, therefore the
 expected rows carry each user's own credit limit next to that user's
 own revenue: Bob 20000 and 7300, Alice 10000 and 8800, Carol 30000
 and 7300, Dave 40000 and 6500, ordered by city first in the pinned
 CCE collation.

 The fifth query filters the fan-out query to product 1 orders. The
 product 1 orders are order 1 (Alice 1500), order 4 (Carol 1500),
 order 7 (Bob 1500), order 10 (Dave 1500), and order 12 (Alice 1500).
 The filter sits inside the revenue sub-aggregation, under the group,
 therefore filtered revenue by city is Springfield 3000 + 1500 =
 4500, Shelbyville 1500, Capital City 1500. A planner that applied
 the filter after aggregation would leave revenue at the unfiltered
 16100, 7300, and 6500 and this test would catch the lie. Credit
 stays 40000, 20000, 40000 because the filter names the orders table
 and credit aggregates users alone. The sixth query filters a column
 the model does not know and must earn diagnostic 27, never a plan.

 The seventh query asks for the average order alongside total credit
 by city. An average cannot be re-aggregated: Springfield's per-user
 averages are Alice 8800 over 4 orders = 2200 and Carol 7300 over 3 =
 2433, and averaging those averages gives 2316, not the true city
 average. The planner therefore carries the average as a sum and a
 count, re-aggregates both as sums, and divides after the combine:
 Springfield 16100 / 7 = 2300, Shelbyville 7300 / 3 = 2433, Capital
 City 6500 / 2 = 3250, integer division throughout. The old planner
 refused this query with diagnostic 25; the decomposition retired
 the code.

 The eighth query reaches two hops: revenue lives on orders, the
 region dimension lives on regions, and the model declares orders to
 users and users to regions, both many-to-one, so the chain is
 grain-safe. Alice and Carol sit in region West, Bob and Dave in
 East, so revenue by region is West 8800 + 7300 = 16100 and East
 7300 + 6500 = 13800. The ninth query runs against a diamond model
 where table t is reachable from fact f through a and through b; the
 planner must refuse with diagnostic 28 naming both paths, never
 pick one silently.

 The tenth and eleventh queries exercise time bucketing. Every order
 carries an order-date in Unix seconds: orders 1 through 6 fall on
 the first through sixth of June 2026 and orders 7 through 12 on the
 first through fifth and the ninth of July 2026, order 12 at noon to
 show the time of day washes out of the bucket. The first of January
 2026 is 1767225600 because fifty-six years of which fourteen are
 leap separate it from the epoch; June the first is 151 days later
 at 1780272000, and July the first is 181 days in at 1782864000. The
 month bucket encodes as year times one hundred plus month, so June
 is 202606 and July 202607. Revenue by month alone is June 1500 +
 5000 + 800 + 1500 + 5000 + 800 = 14600 and July 1500 + 800 + 5000 +
 1500 + 5000 + 1500 = 15300. The eleventh query proves the bucket
 stays grain-correct across a join: revenue by city and month
 derives the bucket on the orders scan, groups the home grain by
 user-id and the bucket alias together, equi-joins users, and
 re-aggregates by city and bucket. June revenue per city: Alice
 1500 + 5000 + 800 with Carol 1500 makes Springfield 8800, Bob 800
 makes Shelbyville 800, Dave 5000 makes Capital City 5000. July:
 Carol 800 + 5000 with Alice 1500 makes Springfield 7300, Bob 1500 +
 5000 makes Shelbyville 6500, Dave 1500 makes Capital City 1500.
 The pinned explain shows the Derive node sitting between the
 filtered scan and the home-grain group.

Section: Star Schema

  users-table : TableDef
  users-table = table-def-with-pk "users" [
    col-def-not-null "user-id" ColInteger,
    col-def-not-null "uname" ColText,
    col-def-not-null "city" ColText,
    col-def-not-null "credit-limit" ColInteger,
    col-def-not-null "region-id" ColInteger
  ] ["user-id"]

  regions-table : TableDef
  regions-table = table-def-with-pk "regions" [
    col-def-not-null "region-id" ColInteger,
    col-def-not-null "region-name" ColText
  ] ["region-id"]

  orders-table : TableDef
  orders-table = table-def-with-pk "orders" [
    col-def-not-null "order-id" ColInteger,
    col-def-not-null "user-id" ColInteger,
    col-def-not-null "product-id" ColInteger,
    col-def-not-null "amount" ColInteger,
    col-def-not-null "order-date" ColInteger
  ] ["order-id"]

  insert-all : Catalog, Text, List RowData, Integer, Integer -> Catalog
  insert-all (cat) (table) (rows) (i) (len) =
    if i >= len then cat
    else let r = catalog-insert-row cat table (list-at rows i)
    in insert-all (r.cir-cat) table rows (i + 1) len

  seed-users : Catalog -> Catalog
  seed-users (cat) =
    let s = table-schema users-table
    in let rows = [
      row-new s [ValInteger 1, ValText "Alice", ValText "Springfield", ValInteger 10000, ValInteger 1],
      row-new s [ValInteger 2, ValText "Bob",   ValText "Shelbyville", ValInteger 20000, ValInteger 2],
      row-new s [ValInteger 3, ValText "Carol", ValText "Springfield", ValInteger 30000, ValInteger 1],
      row-new s [ValInteger 4, ValText "Dave",  ValText "Capital City", ValInteger 40000, ValInteger 2]
    ]
    in insert-all cat "users" rows 0 (list-length rows)

  seed-regions : Catalog -> Catalog
  seed-regions (cat) =
    let s = table-schema regions-table
    in let rows = [
      row-new s [ValInteger 1, ValText "West"],
      row-new s [ValInteger 2, ValText "East"]
    ]
    in insert-all cat "regions" rows 0 (list-length rows)

  seed-orders : Catalog -> Catalog
  seed-orders (cat) =
    let s = table-schema orders-table
    in let rows = [
      row-new s [ValInteger 1,  ValInteger 1, ValInteger 1, ValInteger 1500, ValInteger 1780272000],
      row-new s [ValInteger 2,  ValInteger 1, ValInteger 2, ValInteger 5000, ValInteger 1780358400],
      row-new s [ValInteger 3,  ValInteger 2, ValInteger 3, ValInteger 800,  ValInteger 1780444800],
      row-new s [ValInteger 4,  ValInteger 3, ValInteger 1, ValInteger 1500, ValInteger 1780531200],
      row-new s [ValInteger 5,  ValInteger 4, ValInteger 2, ValInteger 5000, ValInteger 1780617600],
      row-new s [ValInteger 6,  ValInteger 1, ValInteger 3, ValInteger 800,  ValInteger 1780704000],
      row-new s [ValInteger 7,  ValInteger 2, ValInteger 1, ValInteger 1500, ValInteger 1782864000],
      row-new s [ValInteger 8,  ValInteger 3, ValInteger 3, ValInteger 800,  ValInteger 1782950400],
      row-new s [ValInteger 9,  ValInteger 3, ValInteger 2, ValInteger 5000, ValInteger 1783036800],
      row-new s [ValInteger 10, ValInteger 4, ValInteger 1, ValInteger 1500, ValInteger 1783123200],
      row-new s [ValInteger 11, ValInteger 2, ValInteger 2, ValInteger 5000, ValInteger 1783209600],
      row-new s [ValInteger 12, ValInteger 1, ValInteger 1, ValInteger 1500, ValInteger 1783598400]
    ]
    in insert-all cat "orders" rows 0 (list-length rows)

  build-star : Catalog
  build-star =
    let c1 = catalog-create-table catalog-new users-table
    in let c2 = catalog-create-table (c1.cat) orders-table
    in let c3 = catalog-create-table (c2.cat) regions-table
    in seed-regions (seed-orders (seed-users (c3.cat)))

Section: The Model

  users-t : LensTable
  users-t = LensTable { name = "users", primary-key = "user-id", grain = "one row per registered user" }

  orders-t : LensTable
  orders-t = LensTable { name = "orders", primary-key = "order-id", grain = "one row per order" }

  regions-t : LensTable
  regions-t = LensTable { name = "regions", primary-key = "region-id", grain = "one row per sales region" }

  orders-to-users : LensJoin
  orders-to-users = LensJoin { from-table = "orders", to-table = "users", on-left = "user-id", on-right = "user-id", cardinality = ManyToOne }

  users-to-regions : LensJoin
  users-to-regions = LensJoin { from-table = "users", to-table = "regions", on-left = "region-id", on-right = "region-id", cardinality = ManyToOne }

  city-dim : LensDimension
  city-dim = LensDimension { name = "city", table = "users", column = "city", bucket = LbNone }

  uname-dim : LensDimension
  uname-dim = LensDimension { name = "user-name", table = "users", column = "uname", bucket = LbNone }

  product-dim : LensDimension
  product-dim = LensDimension { name = "product", table = "orders", column = "product-id", bucket = LbNone }

  region-dim : LensDimension
  region-dim = LensDimension { name = "region", table = "regions", column = "region-name", bucket = LbNone }

  month-dim : LensDimension
  month-dim = LensDimension { name = "order-month", table = "orders", column = "order-date", bucket = LbMonth }

  revenue-measure : LensMeasure
  revenue-measure = LensMeasure {
    name = "revenue",
    table = "orders",
    column = "amount",
    agg = LensAggSum,
    description = "Sum of order amounts in cents."
  }

  credit-measure : LensMeasure
  credit-measure = LensMeasure {
    name = "total-credit",
    table = "users",
    column = "credit-limit",
    agg = LensAggSum,
    description = "Sum of user credit limits in cents. User grain."
  }

  avg-order-measure : LensMeasure
  avg-order-measure = LensMeasure {
    name = "avg-order",
    table = "orders",
    column = "amount",
    agg = LensAggAvg,
    description = "Average order amount in cents. Order grain."
  }

  sales-model : LensModel
  sales-model = LensModel {
    name = "sales",
    tables = [users-t, orders-t, regions-t],
    joins = [orders-to-users, users-to-regions],
    dimensions = [city-dim, uname-dim, product-dim, region-dim, month-dim],
    measures = [revenue-measure, credit-measure, avg-order-measure]
  }

Section: The Diamond Model

  diamond-model : LensModel
  diamond-model = LensModel {
    name = "diamond",
    tables = [
      LensTable { name = "f", primary-key = "fid", grain = "one row per fact" },
      LensTable { name = "a", primary-key = "aid", grain = "one row per a" },
      LensTable { name = "b", primary-key = "bid", grain = "one row per b" },
      LensTable { name = "t", primary-key = "tid", grain = "one row per t" }
    ],
    joins = [
      LensJoin { from-table = "f", to-table = "a", on-left = "aid", on-right = "aid", cardinality = ManyToOne },
      LensJoin { from-table = "f", to-table = "b", on-left = "bid", on-right = "bid", cardinality = ManyToOne },
      LensJoin { from-table = "a", to-table = "t", on-left = "tid", on-right = "tid", cardinality = ManyToOne },
      LensJoin { from-table = "b", to-table = "t", on-left = "tid", on-right = "tid", cardinality = ManyToOne }
    ],
    dimensions = [LensDimension { name = "tname", table = "t", column = "tname", bucket = LbNone }],
    measures = [LensMeasure { name = "fsum", table = "f", column = "v", agg = LensAggSum, description = "Sum of fact values." }]
  }

Section: Queries

  revenue-by-city-q : LensQuery
  revenue-by-city-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city"], measures = ["revenue"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

  fanout-q : LensQuery
  fanout-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city"], measures = ["total-credit", "revenue"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

  unknown-q : LensQuery
  unknown-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city"], measures = ["profit"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

  two-dim-q : LensQuery
  two-dim-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city", "user-name"], measures = ["total-credit", "revenue"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

  product-filter : LensFilter
  product-filter = LensFilter { table = "orders", column = "product-id", value = LfInt 1 }

  filtered-q : LensQuery
  filtered-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city"], measures = ["total-credit", "revenue"], filters = [product-filter], limit = 0 }

  bad-filter-q : LensQuery
  bad-filter-q = LensQuery {
    lens-name = "sales",
    dimensions = ["city"],
    measures = ["revenue"],
    filters = [LensFilter { table = "orders", column = "discount", value = LfInt 1 }],
    limit = 0
  }

  avg-q : LensQuery
  avg-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city"], measures = ["total-credit", "avg-order"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

  region-q : LensQuery
  region-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["region"], measures = ["revenue"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

  diamond-q : LensQuery
  diamond-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "diamond", dimensions = ["tname"], measures = ["fsum"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

  month-q : LensQuery
  month-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["order-month"], measures = ["revenue"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

  city-month-q : LensQuery
  city-month-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city", "order-month"], measures = ["revenue"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

Section: Display

  fmt-val : ColumnValue -> Text
  fmt-val (v) =
    when v
      is ValInteger (n) -> show n
      is ValText (t) -> t
      is ValBoolean (b) -> if b then "True" else "False"
      is ValNull -> "NULL"

  fmt-vals : List ColumnValue, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  fmt-vals (vals) (i) (len) (acc) =
    if i >= len then acc
    else let v = list-at vals i
    in let sep = if i > 0 then " | " else ""
    in fmt-vals vals (i + 1) len (acc & sep & fmt-val v)

  fmt-rows : List RowData, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  fmt-rows (rows) (i) (len) (acc) =
    if i >= len then acc
    else let row = list-at rows i
    in let line = "  " & fmt-vals (row.values) 0 (list-length (row.values)) ""
    in let sep = if i > 0 then "\n" else ""
    in fmt-rows rows (i + 1) len (acc & sep & line)

  fmt-qr : QueryResult -> Text
  fmt-qr (qr) =
    if qr.qr-ok == False then "ERROR: " & qr.qr-msg
    else fmt-rows (qr.qr-rows) 0 (qr.qr-count) ""

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "=== lens query test: grain-correct planning ==="
    let cat = build-star
    in let revenue-qr = lens-run cat sales-model revenue-by-city-q
    in let fanout-plan = lens-plan sales-model fanout-q
    in let fanout-qr = lens-run cat sales-model fanout-q
    in let bad = lens-plan sales-model unknown-q
    in let two-dim-qr = lens-run cat sales-model two-dim-q
    in let filtered-plan = lens-plan sales-model filtered-q
    in let filtered-qr = lens-run cat sales-model filtered-q
    in let bad-filter = lens-plan sales-model bad-filter-q
    in let avg-qr = lens-run cat sales-model avg-q
    in let region-plan = lens-plan sales-model region-q
    in let region-qr = lens-run cat sales-model region-q
    in let diamond = lens-plan diamond-model diamond-q
    in let month-qr = lens-run cat sales-model month-q
    in let city-month-plan = lens-plan sales-model city-month-q
    in let city-month-qr = lens-run cat sales-model city-month-q
    in act
      print-line-uni "-- revenue by city (city | revenue)"
      print-line-uni (fmt-qr revenue-qr)
      print-line-uni "-- fan-out plan"
      print-line-uni (explain (fanout-plan.plan-op) 0)
      print-line-uni "-- fan-out: credit and revenue by city (city | total-credit | revenue)"
      print-line-uni (fmt-qr fanout-qr)
      print-line-uni "-- unknown measure is a diagnostic, not a plan"
      print-line-uni (lp-render-diags (bad.plan-diags) 0 "")
      print-line-uni "-- two dims, two measures (city | user-name | total-credit | revenue)"
      print-line-uni (fmt-qr two-dim-qr)
      print-line-uni "-- filtered fan-out plan (filter under the revenue group)"
      print-line-uni (explain (filtered-plan.plan-op) 0)
      print-line-uni "-- product 1 only: credit and revenue by city (city | total-credit | revenue)"
      print-line-uni (fmt-qr filtered-qr)
      print-line-uni "-- unknown filter column is a diagnostic, not a plan"
      print-line-uni (lp-render-diags (bad-filter.plan-diags) 0 "")
      print-line-uni "-- grain-correct average across the join (city | total-credit | avg-order)"
      print-line-uni (fmt-qr avg-qr)
      print-line-uni "-- multi-hop plan (orders -> users -> regions)"
      print-line-uni (explain (region-plan.plan-op) 0)
      print-line-uni "-- revenue by region, two hops away (region | revenue)"
      print-line-uni (fmt-qr region-qr)
      print-line-uni "-- two paths to one table is a diagnostic, not a plan"
      print-line-uni (lp-render-diags (diamond.plan-diags) 0 "")
      print-line-uni "-- revenue by month bucket (order-date__month | revenue)"
      print-line-uni (fmt-qr month-qr)
      print-line-uni "-- bucketed plan across a join (derive under the home-grain group)"
      print-line-uni (explain (city-month-plan.plan-op) 0)
      print-line-uni "-- revenue by city and month (city | order-date__month | revenue)"
      print-line-uni (fmt-qr city-month-qr)
      print-line-uni "lens-query-test: done"
    end
  end

